    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_90d29db3",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: thanksgiving_in_china; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a Thanksgiving dinner scene with a roasted turkey, corn, green beans, and other traditional American holiday foods, overlaid with the text 'thanksgiving in china'. This juxtaposition is likely intended to be humorous or satirical, implying that Thanksgiving is an unfamiliar or inappropriate holiday in China. While not overtly abusive or hateful toward any specific group, it may be considered harmful because it reinforces a stereotype that Chinese people do not celebrate or understand Western holidays, potentially contributing to cultural misunderstanding or exoticization. The meme's intent is to create a humorous contrast between American Thanksgiving traditions and Chinese cultural norms, but it risks trivializing or misrepresenting Chinese cultural practices by implying they are irrelevant or foreign to the point of absurdity.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_0e563369"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
